# Public-only option metadata design review

Actual reviewer `/root/research_architect`, 2026-10-10 UTC. Conclusion: **revise the prospective metadata interface before checker/producer use; the nine semantic controls are consistent in principle**. This is a public design critique, with zero candidate, label, implementation, generation or data approval. Preserve metadata1612 and root freezeab948 unchanged; a NEW amendment must become operative before independently frozen source/tests and production.

Exact public evidence: metadata SHA256 `1612b14d7549b7fb406cbef8e127440dcfddaf30548ef29d217bc49aefb6c854` (10,453 bytes); task contract `44652656ad18e60c98c96db14e0a96b4e46b0dad0bd57f257bca30384ab53b3f`; configuration `422f67c836639d0accbf411c3080ef4fc7695ad8630120a140488c90a19061fa`; curriculum `8bda187009cc91756248ddd86792c28aabe0793a3f6be304bb9433bfdf48be34`; canonical schema `f4d8276fe000ceafb0f70c69dbfd1608b823767487d7c0a79623f82cf0daf25f`; root freeze `ab948541d137ec679562f61309b2192277da65f45266cd80443187e06c07b3b0`.

## Interface correction before production

1. Metadata line7 calls `family_claims` an existing canonical field. The allowed public canonical schema neither establishes that field nor `family_control_claims`; it allows additional properties. The configuration does not name a claim container. Root separately reports having inspected the actual pipeline and identified its established container as `family_control_claims`. I have not read that private implementation in this public-only review. Correct the spelling in a NEW prospective amendment to use the established container, and explicitly route the future checker by published source/version bindings. Do not silently amend1612 or grandfather a future candidate with an ignored parallel claim field.
2. Line31 requires both `name` and `property` and an exact six-key claim object. This is explicit, rather than ambiguous, but semantically redundant and an avoidable integration restriction. Prefer a single identifier, `name` OR `property`, with required `scope,evidence_manifest,control_id,pair_sample_ids`. Explicitly permit existing typed optional provenance diagnostics, including `source_family_key` when supplied and verified against actual owner/members. Publish the precise compatible vocabulary before any checker; do not permit arbitrary untyped fields or an undocumented exact-key test. A probe pointer never substitutes for actual pair IDs. No extra per-row status/target is needed.
3. Line35 declares logical manifest source-hash obligations without fixed hash-field spelling, and expressly leaves manifest keys open. A checker must not invent a closed top-level shape or private hash-key alias. A NEW discoverable public source-bindings encoding is advisable: bind factory-relative public paths to their exact SHA256, including task contract/config/original metadata and operative amendment as appropriate. Keep `control_pairs` and its published minimum entry fields. Wrong actual bytes are invalid; optional diagnostics are not automatically mandatory. Do not infer version from sample-ID or generator spelling.

These are prospective interface recommendations, not a retroactive ruling against data. No checker or producer has used1612 according to root's supplied execution boundary.

## Semantic feasibility, with no generated cohort

A small analytic witness demonstrates that the simultaneous cut/guard requirements need not contradict each other. Consider a root whose parameter-dependent initiation remains true at the first cut, a committed nonzero increment, and a call binding a child parameter from the then-current x register. The child initiates while x is below a threshold; a selected branch then increases x past both its entry and branch thresholds. Cut immediately after that effect, with root/child/selected-branch frames active. The saved child parameter remains pending in a later y increment, followed by child return and further caller work. The current child initiation and branch test can now be false, yet resume legitimately retains its entered frame and chosen branch. Restart repeats the already committed root increment before a later child entry can fail; root initiation passes, an actual non-idempotent effect repeats, and terminal status differs from successful resume. This is a permissible replay witness even if the new child later blocks; an immediately blocked root restart is not.

Using small positive thresholds/increments, this skeleton needs two options, one parameter per option, one conditional level, four actual F effects and approximately nine semantic events, well inside the selected24-instruction/48-event bounds. A one-event P budget commits the pending child effect and leaves return/caller work for U. Changing the root's used argument gives A while another value makes one initiation atom fail in I. Changing one root success literal gives S with identical effects. Changing an active checkpoint binding/cursor/state leaf gives X while history remains fixed. A fresh child argument read from a register, then used after x changes, supplies the saved-binding dependency; merely using a constant root argument would not by itself prove that mechanism.

This is analytic consistency reasoning, not an interpreter execution, complete typed toy, source family or future target. It does not prove feasibility of all12 structurally distinct families. The separately authored interpreter and primitive/event simulator must still demonstrate simultaneous controls and every boundary before production, with first failures preserved. The four strata may emphasize different dependencies while every family retains the common cut/guard obligations.

## Counts and explicit owner scope

For12 proposed families and9 contexts x2 renderers:216 correlated records,108 typed control tasks,144train/72exposed-dev rows and8/4 families. Eight within-renderer names give16 entries/family, plus9 field-order entries:300 named pairs total. Nine claims on each216 rows give1,944 claims. Each within-renderer named entry has9 owners; each field-order entry has2. Thus192 within-renderer entries support1,728 claims and108 field-order entries support216 claims. There are1,344 nonmember owner claims among the first eight names. These counts are design arithmetic, not measured data.

Line29's natural reading correctly scopes same-renderer owner binding to the first eight names. State the field-order exception explicitly in the amendment: both members share the owner's family/index/split/context, but their renderers are forward/reverse; each owner may be either member. Do not apply same-renderer equality to both field-order members. Shared IDs across distinct names remain legitimate; require exactly-one lookup by ID, identifier and ordered actual pair, with full record/candidate hash checks and actual execution evidence. All of this is compatible with nonmember owners.

## Clarifications and limits for the later checker

- Replay must be witnessed by the validated original history/F trace and actual T new events. Invocation counters restart, and event after-states may differ; equality of entire historical event objects is not required. Use actual program instruction locators and explicitly define the non-idempotent effect witness. Do not credit zero add, identity scale, idempotent reset, or a swap whose actual operands are equal merely from the opcode name. The same-state/status-difference and actually repeated effect gates remain necessary.
- P/U require normalized exact second snapshots and original history extended by P events; U's suffix is the suffix after that second cut, rather than all of R's new events. Effects before either cut must not be replayed. Budget counts all semantic events, including enter/branch/return, and a terminal event exactly at budget is terminal.
- I/S retain original requirements that every other predicate atom remains true. X must target an active consequential leaf, with stage3 invalid_checkpoint and no new events; an unrelated wrong history would be stage2 invalid_history and is not this control. Malformed diagnostics cannot override validation precedence.
- `property_witnesses` has no newly published row-property enumeration or closed witness subshape here. Do not turn family controls into per-row tags or add private required diagnostic keys without a NEW public definition. Check actual dependency metrics and honest2..4 levels; views/event/frame counts alone do not establish difficulty.
- Publish full-option and shared-primitive normalization rules before checker execution. Preserve relevant argument def/use, shared-register, guard/branch and success dependencies; do not erase them merely because primitive opcodes are legacy. Compare actual target-free legacy inputs and all proposed source graphs. Constant/name/cut/style changes add no family. The12-family novelty claim remains unproven; one feasible skeleton is not12 sources.
- Keep every typed program, ordered event history and checkpoint student-visible. Context/status/claim annotations stay outside Task JSON. Avoid substring bans that reject otherwise legitimate option/parameter names. The complete public semantics are instruction policy, rather than a private per-row outcome.
- Mode/history-length and negative-control correlations are expected. Measure actual status/effect/length and finite-program baselines with coverage/abstentions. All four strata appear in dev, so this is exposed development coverage rather than structural OOD. Neither source/view counts nor exact interpreter correctness establish learned hierarchy, model performance or efficacy.

I authored the original task/curriculum/config and may later adjudicate the data; this public review has design/review overlap. Root supplied the new metadata and actual pipeline-field concern. Same-model/common-guidance risk remains. I inspected only the six listed public artifacts, read their complete text, and used public analytic reasoning; no private producer/oracle/reviewer artifact, RSM candidate or sealed instrument was read. No old/inventoried file or root draft was edited.
